#1061 is fixed and committed as 2fb7c78d. When you Ctrl-C a tool call, the model now just gets Cancelled. It no longer gets "The shell command failed. Check if the command exists…", and the cancel no longer counts as a failure. Build, all tests, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check pass.

Pre-check: no earlier commit had fixed this. The only commit that mentions #1061 is f9d96bc9, the one that filed it.

The fix (src/tool_wrappers.rs, +4 lines): RecoveryHintTool now returns a cancel unchanged, in the same check that already does this for yoyo's own deliberate refusals (#710). So no hint is added and the failure counter isn't bumped. I fixed the comment that listed Cancelled among the errors that get advice, and added a line saying why: the user stopped the call, so nothing failed. The old Cancelled branch below can no longer be reached; it stays only because the compiler requires every error type to be handled, and it returns Cancelled too.

Tests (in src/tool_wrappers_cancel_tests.rs, using a stub tool named bash):
• A cancel comes back as Cancelled, and its full text is exactly "Cancelled".
• A cancel followed by a real failure on the same command gets the first-failure hint. The expected text comes from a fresh wrapper, and a check confirms that text really is the un-escalated version.
• Near-miss: two real failures still get hints, and the second still escalates ("2 times.").

Sabotage check: before the fix, both cancel tests failed by name. Removing the new check (one command, marked NEUTERED, then restored) fails only the counter test. That's because the leftover Cancelled branch on its own still returns the cancel unchanged.

Other places that could report a cancel as a failure: none needed changing. The sub-agent error wrapper in the same file already passes a cancel through without advice, and hooks.rs already returns it unchanged. The other Cancelled in hooks.rs is a test stub, and smart_edit.rs doesn't handle cancels.

Bookkeeping: tool_wrappers.rs went from 5692 to 5696 lines; I updated the size register in tests/module_size.rs with a Day 235 note and added a dated line to the ARCHITECTURE.md entry for the file. The commit touches 4 files, including those two. git grep '#1061' finds only code comments, so no user-facing message points at the ticket.

One slip on the way: I ran two edits to the same file in parallel, and the second overwrote the first. A test run showed it, and I re-applied the lost edit on its own.
